.TH TRIES 1 "May 2026" "tries 5.0.0" "User Commands"


.SH NAME
tries \- build a character or token trie from text and emit Graphviz DOT

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tries
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIfile\fR ...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tries
reads lines of text from files or standard input and builds a trie
(prefix tree), emitting the result as Graphviz DOT to standard output.

In the default character mode each character is a node.
In token mode
.RB ( \-D )
each delimited segment is a node, which is better suited to IPs, paths,
and URLs.

Graphviz
.RB ( dot )
is required only to render the DOT output into PDF, PNG, or SVG.
.B tries
itself has no Python dependencies beyond the standard library.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS Input
.TP
.I file ...
One or more input files. If omitted, read from standard input unless a
.B \-\-sample\-*
flag is used.

.TP
.B \-\-sample\-hosts
Include built-in sample hostnames.

.TP
.B \-\-sample\-ips
Include built-in sample IPv4 addresses.

.TP
.B \-\-sample\-paths
Include built-in sample UNIX directory paths.

.TP
.B \-\-sample\-urls
Include built-in sample URLs.

.TP
.B \-\-sample\-emails
Include built-in sample email addresses.

.TP
.B \-\-sample\-nato
Include built-in sample NATO phonetic words.

Sample flags may be combined with each other and with file or stdin input.

.SS Filtering
.TP
.BI \-f " REGEX" ", \-\-filter " REGEX
Keep only lines matching REGEX (case-sensitive). Default: \fB.*\fR (keep all).

.TP
.B \-\-invert\-filter
Invert the filter: keep lines that do \fInot\fR match.

.SS Trie mode
.TP
.BI \-D " CHAR" ", \-\-delim " CHAR
Split each input line on CHAR and build a token-based trie instead of a
character-level trie. Use \fB.\fR for IPs, \fB/\fR for paths and URLs,
\fB@\fR for emails.

.TP
.B \-\-rtl
Reverse token order after splitting. Only applies in token mode.
Useful for email addresses and domain names where the hierarchy reads
right-to-left (e.g.\& \fBcom \(-> example \(-> user\fR).

.SS Marking
.TP
.BI \-M " PATTERN" " [" PATTERN " ...]" ", \-\-mark " PATTERN " ..."
Regex patterns used to mark terminal nodes with the mark colour.
Case-sensitive. Defaults:
.BR new ", " old ", " oob ", " ilo ", " trap ", " traps ", " "lm[0-9][0-9]$" .
Pass \fB\-M ''\fR to disable all marking.

.SS Normalisation
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-prefix
Keep the Windows \fBDOMAIN\e\fRhost prefix. Default is to strip it.

.TP
.B \-\-keep\-fqdn
Keep the full DNS name. Default is to strip everything after the first dot
(e.g.\& \fBserver01.domain.local\fR becomes \fBserver01\fR).

.TP
.BI \-i ", \-\-ignore\-case"
Normalise internal node IDs to lowercase. Labels retain their original case.

.SS Display
.TP
.B \-H ", \-\-head"
Render the first-character node as a filled circle. Ignored in token mode.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-labels
Remove labels from terminal and head nodes.

.TP
.BI \-d " {LR,TB}" ", \-\-dir " {LR,TB}
Graph direction. \fBLR\fR = left-to-right (default), \fBTB\fR = top-to-bottom.

.SS Output
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" ", \-\-output " FILE
Write DOT output to FILE instead of standard output.

.SS Themes and colours
.TP
.BI \-T " NAME" ", \-\-theme " NAME
Apply a named colour theme. Use \fB\-\-list\-themes\fR to see available names.
Default: \fBdefault\fR.

.TP
.BI \-F " NAME" ", \-\-font " NAME
Font family for node labels. Choices:
.BR courier ", " courier-new ", " dejavu ", " liberation ", " nimbus ", " helvetica ", " menlo ", " consolas .
Default: \fBcourier\fR.

.TP
.BI \-cn " COLOUR" ", \-\-color\-normal " COLOUR
Override the theme colour for normal terminal nodes.

.TP
.BI \-cm " COLOUR" ", \-\-color\-mark " COLOUR
Override the theme colour for marked terminal nodes.

.TP
.BI \-ch " COLOUR" ", \-\-color\-head " COLOUR
Override the theme colour for head nodes.

.TP
.BI \-ce " COLOUR" ", \-\-color\-edge " COLOUR
Override the theme colour for edges.

.TP
.BI \-cp " COLOUR" ", \-\-color\-point " COLOUR
Override the theme colour for internal point nodes.

.TP
.BI \-tn " COLOUR" ", \-\-text\-normal " COLOUR
Override the label text colour for normal terminal nodes.

.TP
.BI \-tm " COLOUR" ", \-\-text\-mark " COLOUR
Override the label text colour for marked terminal nodes.

.TP
.BI \-th " COLOUR" ", \-\-text\-head " COLOUR
Override the label text colour for head nodes.

All colours use the X11/Graphviz palette (e.g.\& \fBcornsilk2\fR,
\fBpalegreen3\fR, \fBroyalblue3\fR). See
.UR https://graphviz.org/doc/info/colors.html
.UE .

.SS Theme management
.TP
.B \-\-list\-themes
List available theme names and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-dump\-themes
Print the merged THEMES and FONT_MAP dicts to stdout and exit. Useful as a
starting point for a custom \fBthemes.py\fR.

.TP
.BI \-\-save\-theme " NAME"
Save the current colour and font settings as a reusable theme called NAME.
Writes to \fBthemes_custom.py\fR in the XDG data directory
(\fB~/.local/share/tries/\fR by default).

.SS Info
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-debug
Write debug information to standard error.

.SH EXAMPLES
Build a trie from a file and render to PDF:
.PP
.RS
.EX
tries servers.txt | dot \-Tpdf \-o trie.pdf
.EE
.RE

Use the built-in hostname sample with head nodes and midnight theme:
.PP
.RS
.EX
tries \-\-sample\-hosts \-H \-T midnight | dot \-Tpng \-o hosts.png
.EE
.RE

Token-mode trie of IP addresses split on dots:
.PP
.RS
.EX
tries \-\-sample\-ips \-D . | dot \-Tpdf \-o ips.pdf
.EE
.RE

Emails in reverse token order (domain \(-> user):
.PP
.RS
.EX
tries \-\-sample\-emails \-D @ \-\-rtl | dot \-Tpng \-o emails.png
.EE
.RE

Filter to firewall hosts only, marking out-of-band nodes:
.PP
.RS
.EX
tries \-f fw \-M oob servers.txt | dot \-Tpdf \-o fw.pdf
.EE
.RE

Save a custom theme:
.PP
.RS
.EX
tries \-cn lightskyblue1 \-cm mediumspringgreen \-ch royalblue3 \e
    \-\-save\-theme electric\-dusk
.EE
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tries/themes.py
Installed theme and font definitions. Merged over the built-in defaults.

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tries/themes_custom.py
User-defined custom themes written by \fB\-\-save\-theme\fR.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PREFIX
If set to a path other than \fB$HOME\fR, support files are loaded from
\fI$PREFIX/share/tries/\fR instead of the XDG data directory.

.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Overrides the XDG base directory for support files (default:
\fI~/.local/share\fR).

